  "seoTitle": "Fire Destroys 41 Houses In Baduy Luar Settlement Of Banten",
  "metaDescription": "A large blaze in the Baduy Luar settlement in Lebak, Banten, has destroyed 41 houses and multiple food storage barns. Authorities are responding.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "A total of 41 houses and several food storage barns were destroyed in the Cipaler Babakan area of the Baduy Luar settlement.",
    "The fire reportedly started on Thursday night, with initial investigations suggesting it may have been caused by a cooking stove.",
    "Local government officials have been directed to provide emergency assistance to the displaced residents in the Lebak district."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A significant fire broke out in the Baduy Luar indigenous settlement, located within the Kanekes village of Lebak, Banten, on the night of November 19, 2026. Reports indicate that the blaze devastated the community, resulting in the destruction of 41 residential homes, traditional food barns, and other communal structures. While initial assessments provided varying figures regarding the scale of the damage, recent reports confirmed the loss of over 40 units. Local authorities, including the regional leadership, have initiated efforts to support the displaced community members. Preliminary findings from ongoing investigations suggest that the incident may have originated from a cooking stove used by a resident. This event has prompted an urgent call for rapid response measures from the provincial government to address the immediate needs of the affected population in the Baduy region.",
